{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בן פורת יוסף", :translit "ben porat yosef", :gloss "a fruitful son, Joseph"} {:he "בן פורת", :translit "ben porat", :gloss "a fruitful son"} {:he "מנשה ואפרים", :translit "menashe ve'efrayim", :gloss "Manasseh and Ephraim"} {:he "בן פותר", :translit "ben poter", :gloss "a son who interprets"} {:he "פתרון חלומות", :translit "pitron chalomot", :gloss "interpretation of dreams"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "בן פורת", :b "מנשה ואפרים"} {:kind :other, :note "Switching of letters reshapes בן פורת into בן פותר ('a son who interprets')"}], :frame {:text "The decree of hard labor over Israel is traced to Joseph: the Egyptians set officers over them, as stated at Exodus 1:11. The same root פרך appears in the charge of Leviticus 25:43 not to rule over a fellow with rigor, linking the two verses. The gematria of בן פורת equaling מנשה ואפרים is the teacher's own structural observation.", :sources ["Exodus 1:11" "Leviticus 25:43"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בנות צעדה עלי שור", :translit "benot tza'adah alai shur", :gloss "daughters tread upon the wall"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reversal: שור ('wall') read as רשף ('arrow'), and בנות as בנה ('built'), yielding 'the wall built against the arrow'"}], :frame {:text "Midrashic tradition reads בנות צעדה עלי שור as a prophecy of Israel's future wars. The battle of Jericho is described at Joshua 6:20, where the wall falls after the people shout.", :sources ["Joshua 6:20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "בן פורת", :a-value 738, :b "מנשה ואפרים", :b-value 732, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Switching of letters reshapes בן פורת into בן פותר ('a son who interprets')", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Reversal: שור ('wall') read as רשף ('arrow'), and בנות as בנה ('built'), yielding 'the wall built against the arrow'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :discipline "bht-